From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 12:10:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: report the tallest frame the macroblock limit
 allows on AR50_LITE

VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES reports the platform's width and height limits,
but AR50_LITE also limits a frame to 8160 macroblocks (1920x1088), which
a stepwise range cannot express: it reports 128x128 - 1920x1920.

A client that checks only the reported bounds takes the decoder for
streams it cannot decode. Chromium's V4L2 decoder does: it would send
Steam's 1920x1200 VP9 startup movies (9000 macroblocks) to the decoder
instead of to software.

On platforms that set framesizes_fit_mbpf (only AR50_LITE here), report
the tallest frame that fits at the widest width instead. Portrait frames
taller than that leave the reported range, although the hardware could
decode them.

The same change as our venus patch of 2026-11-22, which this replaces now
that iris drives the SM6115.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h     |    2 ++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu_ar50lt.c |    1 +
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c                |   12 ++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h
@@ -348,6 +348,8 @@ struct iris_platform_data {
 	u32 num_vpp_pipe;
 	bool no_aon;
 	bool no_rpmh;
+	/* Report only frame sizes that fit inst_caps->max_mbpf. */
+	bool framesizes_fit_mbpf;
 	u32 wd_intr_mask;
 	u32 icc_ib_multiplier;
 	u32 max_session_count;
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu_ar50lt.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu_ar50lt.c
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ const struct iris_platform_data qcm2290_data = {
 	.tz_cp_config_data_size = ARRAY_SIZE(tz_cp_config_ar50lt),
 	.num_vpp_pipe = 1,
 	.no_rpmh = true,
+	.framesizes_fit_mbpf = true,
 	.wd_intr_mask = WRAPPER_INTR_STATUS_A2HWD_BMSK,
 	.icc_ib_multiplier = 2,
 	.max_session_count = 8,
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vidc.c
@@ -397,6 +397,7 @@ static int iris_enum_framesizes(struct file *filp, voi
 {
 	struct iris_inst *inst = iris_get_inst(filp);
 	struct platform_inst_caps *caps;
+	u32 cols, rows;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (fsize->index)
@@ -419,6 +420,17 @@ static int iris_enum_framesizes(struct file *filp, voi
 	fsize->stepwise.min_height = caps->min_frame_height;
 	fsize->stepwise.max_height = caps->max_frame_height;
 	fsize->stepwise.step_height = STEP_HEIGHT;
+
+	/*
+	 * A stepwise range cannot express the macroblocks-per-frame limit, so
+	 * report the tallest frame that fits it at the widest width.
+	 */
+	if (inst->core->iris_platform_data->framesizes_fit_mbpf) {
+		cols = DIV_ROUND_UP(caps->max_frame_width, 16);
+		rows = caps->max_mbpf / cols;
+		if (rows * 16 < fsize->stepwise.max_height)
+			fsize->stepwise.max_height = rows * 16;
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
